<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK retail is under pressure from every direction - rising costs, changing customer expectations, and competition from global e-commerce giants. The retailers winning right now are the ones using data and automation to operate leaner and serve customers better. Yet many UK retailers still run on a patchwork of legacy POS systems, disconnected spreadsheets, and accounting software that wasn't built for multi-site retail operations.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf retail software compounds the problem. Generic POS packages force you to adapt your product taxonomy, pricing rules, and promotions to their structure. Inventory tools handle simple stock counts but choke on size, colour, and style variants across multiple stores. Loyalty programmes built into POS systems are rigid - one structure fits all, with no scope for tiered rewards, personalised offers, or integration with your e-commerce platform. Staff scheduling add-ons don't account for your footfall patterns or the specific skills each shift requires. The result is store managers spending hours reconciling spreadsheets and buyers making replenishment decisions on stale data.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK retailers that connects your POS, inventory, loyalty, staff scheduling, and supplier management into a single, coherent system. We understand retail operations - from the shop floor to the buying office - and we build software that integrates with your existing POS, accounting, and e-commerce platforms. Whether it's a bespoke loyalty programme that rewards customers across in-store and online channels, or an inventory system that tracks stock by variant across every store in real time, bespoke software fits your exact processes.</p>
<p>Retail compliance adds another layer of complexity. PCI-DSS payment security, GDPR data protection for customer loyalty data, and age-restricted sales verification all demand robust systems. Bespoke software gives you complete control over how customer data is stored, processed, and retained - with audit trails, role-based access, and age verification prompts built in from the start rather than bolted on through a third-party plugin.</p>
<p>A UK fashion retailer with twelve stores was struggling to maintain accurate stock levels across locations, leading to lost sales when online orders referenced stock that had already sold in-store. We built a bespoke inventory sync system that updated stock across all stores and the e-commerce site in real time, with automated reorder alerts based on sell-through rates per store. Within four months, stock accuracy improved from 78% to 99%, online order fulfilment rates increased by 15%, and the buying team reduced overstock on slow-moving lines by 22%.</p>
<p>Retail is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear, measurable ROI. The data is already being generated by your POS, your inventory, and your customer transactions. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into automated replenishment, personalised customer experiences, and real-time visibility across every store and channel.</p>

